875. Koko Eating Bananas
Koko loves to eat bananas. There are n piles of bananas, the ith pile has piles[i] bananas. The guards have gone and will come back in h hours.
Koko can decide her bananas-per-hour eating speed of k. Each hour, she chooses some pile of bananas and eats k bananas from that pile. 
If the pile has less than k bananas, she eats all of them instead and will not eat any more bananas during this hour.
Koko likes to eat slowly but still wants to finish eating all the bananas before the guards return.
Return the minimum integer k such that she can eat all the bananas within h hours.

Explanation:

THe ideology behind is there is an array of bananans. Each element in the array is the pile of bananas available.
what we do is we have to find the rate of time it takes to eat all the bananas such that it is less than h.

For that what we do is we setup an imaginary array where we have the langest possble time (that is eating the maximum piles in the array) and shorted time( which is 1).
We use binary search, take out the mid element as the assumed rate of bananas, calculate the total time based on it and comparing it with h.

Code:

class Solution {
    public int minEatingSpeed(int[] piles, int h) {
        int n= piles.length;

        int left=1; int right=0;
        for(int num:piles){
            right=Math.max(num,right);
        }
        int ans=right;
        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;
            long th=func(piles,mid);
            if(th<=(long)h){
                ans=mid;
                right=mid-1;
            }
            else{
                left=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }

    public static long func(int[] nums, int i){
        long total_hours=0;
        for(int num:nums){
            total_hours+= (num+i-1)/i;
        }
        return total_hours;
    }
}
